<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    ========================================================================
    WorldMapReadability_Ashkarr.xml    Jawa_Patches - authored 2026-08-23
    ========================================================================
    🔴 Owner, 2026-08-23: "make the worldmap faction icons twice as big".

    🔑 THE ENGINE MULTIPLIES A FLAT 30 px BY THIS FIELD, so "twice as big" is
    literally the number 2. `ExpandableWorldObjectsUtility.cs:212`:

        float num = 30f * o.def.expandingIconDrawSize;

    and `WorldObjectDef.cs:88` defaults the field to `1f`. ⇒ Settlement icons
    are drawn at 30 px today and 60 px after this.

    ⚠️ IT IS AN ADD, NOT A REPLACE, AND THAT IS MEASURED. Core's `Settlement`
    WorldObjectDef (`Core/Defs/WorldObjectDefs/WorldObjects.xml`) declares
    `expandingIcon`, `expandingIconPriority`, `fullyExpandedInSpace` and
    `canBePlayerHome` - and NO `expandingIconDrawSize`. A Replace would match
    nothing, and ⛔ a PatchOperationReplace that matches nothing is a RED ERROR
    while a Conditional that matches nothing is SILENT. The Conditional here
    takes the add branch today and would take the replace branch if Ludeon ever
    adds the field, so it survives an update either way.

    ⛔ SCOPE IS `Settlement` ONLY, deliberately. Every WorldObjectDef carries
    this field and several already set their own - Core sets 1.6 on one, Odyssey
    sets 1.35 on three and 1.1 on another. Those are hand-tuned relative sizes
    and doubling them all would flatten the hierarchy the game uses to say which
    objects matter. The owner asked for the FACTION icons; the faction icon on
    the planet is `Settlement.ExpandingIcon => Faction.def.FactionIcon`
    (`Settlement.cs:40`), so `Settlement` is the whole of the ask.

    🔑 The icons this enlarges are the ones that gained a black ring the same
    day - see `outline_faction_icons.py`. The ring was sized at 7 px on a 128 px
    source against a ~30 px draw; at 60 px it reads twice as thick, which is
    the intent, not a defect.
    ========================================================================
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/WorldObjectDef[defName="Settlement"]/expandingIconDrawSize</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/WorldObjectDef[defName="Settlement"]/expandingIconDrawSize</xpath>
      <value><expandingIconDrawSize>2</expandingIconDrawSize></value>
    </match>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/WorldObjectDef[defName="Settlement"]</xpath>
      <value><expandingIconDrawSize>2</expandingIconDrawSize></value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
